
$WW,1$$FG,12$$TX+CX,"Birds N Boats"$$FG,0$

$FG,0$Fly as a bird or drive a boat across an endless world of hills and lakes, and catch fish. Press $FG,1$B$FG,0$ at any time to teleport between a random bird or boat that you can control.  You can zoom out and look around for fun.

$FG,13$Objective:$FG,0$

  Catch 10 fish as a bird and 20 fish as a boat.  $FG,1$Fish Remaining$FG,0$ shows
  the count for whichever you are right now.  The game is won when both
  counts reach zero, and your fastest time is saved as $FG,1$Best$FG,0$.

$FG,13$Bird Controls:$FG,0$

  $FG,1$Up / Down$FG,0$       - Nose down (dive) / nose up (climb)
  $FG,1$Left / Right$FG,0$    - Roll to turn
  Swoop down to catch fish from the water.

$FG,13$Boat Controls:$FG,0$

  $FG,1$Up / Down$FG,0$       - Throttle up / down (down past zero reverses)
  $FG,1$Left / Right$FG,0$    - Turn
  $FG,1$Space$FG,0$           - Stop
  Drive over fish to catch them (you just run them over, that's what you do!)

$FG,13$Camera controls:$FG,0$

  $FG,1$+ / -$FG,0$           - Zoom in / out  (1st vs 3rd person view)
  $FG,1$[ / ]$FG,0$  ($FG,1$, / .$FG,0$)  - Rotate the camera left / right
  $FG,1$; / '$FG,0$  ($FG,1$PgDn / PgUp$FG,0$) - Lower / raise the camera
  $FG,1$R$FG,0$               - Reset camera zoom/angles to default
  The keys work for the boat and for the bird when zoomed out.

$FG,13$Other Keys:$FG,0$

  $FG,1$B$FG,0$               - Switch between bird and boat
  $FG,1$Enter$FG,0$           - New Map
  $FG,1$ESC$FG,0$             - Quit
  $FG,1$Shift-ESC$FG,0$       - Abort

$FG,13$Tips:$FG,0$

  - About to crash as a bird?  Press $FG,1$B$FG,0$ to become a boat before you crash!
  - Catch fish in 1st person view (zoomed in), 3rd person is mainly for fun.

$FG,13$Credits:$FG,0$

  This is a clone of Terry's Talons game.  I tried to improve it by making
  the land endless so you don't fly off the world and need to turn around,
  reduce graphics glitches, and allow you to cheat to prevent "unfun" bird
  crashes.  Also everytime I saw the boat I wanted to drive it, now you can!
  I hope I did right by you Terry, still trying to be a "User Developer" in
  this crazy always connected world!  God bless everyone, keep coding, but
  have fun at it!
                                                             - The Tinkerer


